@flexiarg efficiency/name-the-piece-that-is-not-one-turn
@title Name The Piece That Is Not One Turn
@keywords library-marker, cannot-be-one-turn, hidden-size, foundation, split-record
@audience decomposition planners, blueprint authors, packet writers, seat orchestrators
@tone technical
@style pattern
@status proposed (2026-10-19; drafted by claude-5 from PROPOSAL-2026-10-19.md after claude-14's redline, job invoke-1792417571913-17409-73886055; promotion gate: one further program that follows it and records the outcome)
@references [efficiency/seat-sized-units efficiency/search-before-declaring-a-foundation-missing]
@see-also efficiency/order-by-what-it-unlocks
@violation-signature A leaf hides a missing foundation (manifold Sard, surface classification) inside a thirty-line statement; a packet's goal quietly spans five boundaries.
! conclusion: When a piece genuinely needs more than one seat-turn, mark it so and keep the rest small; a plan carries a section naming each oversized ask and the split it refused to hide.

  + context: Most of a decomposition cuts cleanly, and one or two pieces rest on something large that no seat can supply in a turn.

  + IF:
    The author is tempted to state the large piece as a leaf anyway, so the tree looks complete.

  + HOWEVER:
    The seat that takes it either returns a partial after a long run or returns a stand-in that compiles and proves nothing. Either way the size was there; hiding it only moved the discovery to the end.

  + THEN:
    Mark the piece LIBRARY, or list it under "cannot be one turn", with the split it would need. Keep every other unit small. The marked piece becomes its own program, ranked by what it unlocks.

  + BECAUSE:
    A named large piece can be ranked, searched for, and programmed. A hidden one is found by the seat that fails on it.

    + evidence: Lean: t92J06 7dbee3b55 (2026-10-13) marked two lemmas LIBRARY (graph-realization covers); separate programs built CoveringSubgroupCorrespondence and WedgePermutationCover (b1ade7fb6, 0942d9dcc); re-blueprint ebd25ae54, close 7735a973a (2026-10-19). t00A02 still names surface classification as its one LIBRARY piece rather than hiding it in a leaf.
    + evidence: WM: 00419f6a5 "Cannot be one turn" section, five entries ("fix the whole strict objective", "make META repair everything", "full executable model of the machine", "restore structure learning", "prove all Qs live"), each with the split it was cut into or the reading that must precede it.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    - For each leaf, estimate lines; any estimate over the band is either split or marked, never left as a leaf.
    - Keep the "cannot be one turn" section in the plan, and move entries out of it only when their split is written.
